title: Media Strategy
new-page: true
is-card: true
card-image: img/party.svg
tags: party_affairs
view-if: media_timer <= 0
on-arrival: media_timer = 4; month_actions += 1

= Media Strategy

Television decides elections now. Our research says voters respect you but don't warm to you, and many still can't picture you as Prime Minister.

- @coaching: Voice and presentation coaching.
- @tabloids: Court the tabloids.
- @broadcast: A party political broadcast.
- @interview: A long, serious television interview.
- @easy_discard

@coaching
subtitle: -1 resource
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Requires 1 resource.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; thatcher_rating += 4

A lower voice, a softer hairstyle and fewer hats. You resent every minute of it, and it works.

@tabloids
subtitle: -1 resource
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Requires 1 resource.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; c2_con += 3*(1-dissent); de_con += 2*(1-dissent); tabloid_support += 1

Lunches with editors and an interview in the Sun. Its readers are the skilled workers who voted Labour last time, and some of them are listening.

@broadcast
on-arrival: thatcher_rating += 2 if saatchi_hired; c1_con += 2*(1-dissent) if saatchi_hired; c2_con += 2*(1-dissent) if saatchi_hired; c1_con += 1*(1-dissent) if not saatchi_hired

[? if saatchi_hired : Saatchi & Saatchi make it look more like an advert than a lecture, and people actually watch it. ?][? if not saatchi_hired : It is earnest, worthy and a little dull. ?]

@interview
on-arrival: economic_liberalism += 2; thatcher_rating += 2 if thatcher_rating >= 40; thatcher_rating -= 1 if thatcher_rating < 40; dry_strength += 1

An hour of hard questions on economics. [? if thatcher_rating >= 40 : You are formidable on detail, and it shows. ?][? if thatcher_rating < 40 : You win the argument and lose the audience; you come across as hectoring. ?]
